 r"I am writing to apply for the Graduate Product Analyst position at NCR Atleos in Dundee. I recently completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. Across my academic and professional experience I have worked on understanding what users and clients actually need, turning that into clear requirements and measures, and turning the result into a recommendation someone could act on. I am particularly interested in this role because it sits between business needs and technology, which is where I have done my best work so far.",

 r"What attracts me most to NCR Atleos is that the products have a visible end point: people being able to access cash and banking services reliably, wherever they are. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved. The posting describes analysing customer and market requirements and supporting product strategy and roadmaps, and that is the kind of analysis I want to build my career on.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I mine merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python to find the growth and operations drivers behind the UK marketplace, and I build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that commercial and operations teams use to set targets and track initiatives. Working with product, operations and commercial stakeholders is the normal shape of my week, and the recurring lesson has been that the first metric someone asks for is rarely the one that answers their question. I also used Claude Code to build an AI agent that automates repetitive steps of my own analytics workflow, which my team and partner teams now use; the difficult part was deciding which steps it should own.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology I worked as a Data Scientist Intern on a medical AI product for a pharmaceutical client. I turned the client's expectations for safe answers into a 246-question benchmark and a six-dimension rubric, which they adopted as their acceptance standard, then built a Python pipeline calling six LLM APIs to test the product and ran blinded A/B tests of a medically reviewed knowledge graph. Agreeing what good looks like before testing is the habit I would bring to gathering and prioritising requirements at NCR Atleos.",

 r"My MSc dissertation applied predictive and causal machine learning to 458,840 UK Biobank participants and was delivered as an interactive Streamlit application so that non-specialists could explore the results without touching the code. That project taught me to design a tool around the person using it rather than around the model.",

 r"At Ipsos Strategy3 I researched emerging health-product markets, built market-sizing and forecasting models, structured more than 80 healthcare professional interviews into quantitative data, and turned the analysis into reports and recommendations for client stakeholders. That is where I learned to present a finding to an audience who wants the implication rather than the method.",

 r"I should be clear about one gap. I have not yet worked in financial technology or on a product team that ships hardware and software to banks and retailers. My analysis, requirements and stakeholder foundations are solid and I learn new domains quickly, but I would be learning the payments and self-service landscape in my first months rather than arriving with it.",

 r"I would bring NCR Atleos strong SQL and Python, experience translating stakeholder needs into measurable requirements, market research and modelling skills, and the habit of checking whether something actually works before recommending it. I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029 without sponsorship. I am currently based in London and am happy to relocate to Dundee for the June 2027 start.",

 r"Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my experience in analysis, requirements and stakeholder communication could contribute to NCR Atleos' product teams.",
